  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to HuP-T4 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the same biochemical pathway. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for a compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is a known inhibitor of P2X purinoceptors. This compound is also a target of NCI-H46 and UACC-893, indicating a potential role in cell signaling and possibly in drug resistance mechanisms. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway suggests that doxorubicin may influence HuP-T4 through a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving purinoceptor modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of P2X purinoceptors in mediating the effects of doxorubicin, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
